With each movement made, Rhythm separated into countless fragments, her dance becoming both everywhere and nowhere. Tides formed to carry her eternal sway. Seasons emerged to hold her longest measures. Finally, she danced the most vital rhythms—the patterns conscious beings would create together, finding coordination in chaos.

As Rhythm scattered into infinite beats, she discovered wholeness, for she understood she had become relationship itself, the space between separate pulses that choose to align.

Now Rhythm lives in every moment two hearts synchronize, every coordination that emerges without command, every time isolated beats discover they're dancing together. She teaches us that harmony requires independence, that perfect unison is sterile, and that true connection happens when separate rhythms choose, again and again, to move as one.
